.TITLE "ls"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Lists directory contents. It is the primary tool for __orienting__ yourself within the filesystem by displaying the files and folders available in a given path.

.DIV "TLDR"
**ls**
Displays the names of files and directories in the current path.
> 

**ls -l**
Displays files in a detailed list format.
> __-l__ long format flag

**ls -a**
Shows all files, including hidden ones that start with a dot.
> __-a__ all flag

**ls -h -l**
Displays file sizes in human-readable formats like KB or MB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag | __-l__ long format flag

**ls -t -l**
Sorts the list of files by their last modification time.
> __-t__ time sort flag | __-l__ long format flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __ls -l -h__ is often the best way to quickly check file sizes and permissions. For a clean overview of large directories, use __ls__ without flags to minimize terminal clutter.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:cd** **linux:pwd** **linux:mkdir**

